				<Color>-16777216</Color>
				<Text><![CDATA[This model simulates the basic set of operations of a grain terminal.

These operations are:
- grain unloading from an incoming auto to auto silos.
- grain unloading from a train
- grain unloading from main silos to a ship

Grain unloading from an incoming auto to auto silos.
The auto waits until a suitable line of auto silos become available. After this an auto silo is selected using the following criteria:
 - it is empty or contains the same type of grain as the type being unloaded;
 - there is no operation like unloading to main silos in progress.

After an auto silo is filled to 75% of its capacity, the grain unloading process to main silos is started.

Grain unloading from a train
The train delivers grain and the unloading process to main silos is started immediately. 
Each train and auto delivers only one type of grain. The unloading process from a train and auto silos can happen simultaneously.

Both main silo and auto silos are considered vacant (and thus can be used for loading or unloading) in the following situations:
 - it is empty or contains the same type of grain as the type in question;
 - it is not being loaded or unloaded (i.e. the silo cannot be loaded and unloaded at the same time).

Grain unloading from main silos to a ship
 - The ship berths to one of available piers
 - The ship includes several bilges.
 - Each bilge can contain only one type of grain, however the grain types in different bilges can be different.
 - The ships on different piers can be loaded simultaneously.]]></Text>
